# Security and privacy

- Clinical data is sensitive. Minimize data in responses, logs and external providers.
- UI hiding is never authorization.
- No secrets in client modules or NEXT_PUBLIC variables.
- Never log transcripts, clinical working notes, AI clinical prompt bodies, Google refresh tokens or Twilio auth tokens.
- Sensitive mutations require authenticated user, authorization and audit where applicable.
- Use signed short-lived Storage URLs.
- Before recording/transcription/clinical-AI provider calls, enforce server-side consent state as defined by the product.
- Refusal/revocation of AI/recording/transcription must block the applicable provider flow without impairing ordinary clinical care.
- Do not auto-write AI output into the clinical record without explicit human action.
- Destructive/LGPD flows require explicit confirmation and documented retention behavior.
